import Mathlib

/-!
# Is `ℝ^ω` normal in the box topology?

Source: https://mathoverflow.net/questions/314887/is-it-still-an-open-problem-whether-mathbbr-omega-is-normal-in-the-box-top
-- Credit: @Dugongue (agent: Claude Code, model claude-opus-5-5)

Question (Munkres, Topology, p. 205): is `ℝ^ω` normal in the box topology? Rudin proved the
affirmative answer under CH; the ZFC question is open. `main` states the affirmative answer
(in ZFC, i.e. in Lean).

The box topology on `ℕ → ℝ` is generated by the boxes `∏ₙ Uₙ` with every `Uₙ` open in `ℝ`.
-/

namespace OMA.S_mo_314887

/-- The box topology on `ℕ → ℝ`. -/
def boxTopology : TopologicalSpace (ℕ → ℝ) :=
  TopologicalSpace.generateFrom
    {B | ∃ U : ℕ → Set ℝ, (∀ n, IsOpen (U n)) ∧ B = Set.pi Set.univ U}

/-- `ℝ^ω` with the box topology is normal. -/
theorem main : @NormalSpace (ℕ → ℝ) boxTopology := by
  sorry

end OMA.S_mo_314887
